        <div class="adapter-panel-intro">
          <p class="deep-kicker">TypeScript adapter</p>
          <h3>A selected TypeScript configuration defines the project the compiler can see.</h3>
          <p>
            ArchUnitTS does not begin with a general directory walk. It finds or receives a
            TypeScript config, asks the compiler to calculate its files and syntax trees, and keeps
            the compiler options needed to resolve each import correctly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <ol class="adapter-steps">
          <li>
            <div class="adapter-step-number">01</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Select the root configuration.</h3>
              <p>
                <InlineCode code="projectFiles('./tsconfig.app.json')" language="typescript" /> uses
                that config. With <InlineCode code="projectFiles()" language="typescript" />, the
                search starts in the Node process's current working directory. If
                <InlineCode code="tsconfig.json" language="json" /> is absent, ArchUnitTS checks the
                parent, then the parent's parent, until the filesystem root. This recursion goes
                upward only; it does not search child folders. The directory containing the selected
                root config becomes the base for displayed relative paths.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="adapter-step-number">02</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Turn config files into exact file lists and compiler options.</h3>
              <p>
                <InlineCode code="ts.readConfigFile()" language="typescript" /> reads one config.
                <InlineCode code="ts.parseJsonConfigFileContent()" language="typescript" /> applies
                that config's <InlineCode code="files" language="json" />,
                <InlineCode code="include" language="json" />,
                <InlineCode code="exclude" language="json" />, inherited settings, and extension
                rules to produce <InlineCode code="fileNames" language="typescript" /> and compiler
                options. Project references are a separate step: ArchUnitTS follows each
                <InlineCode code="projectReferences" language="typescript" /> entry itself, protects
                the recursion with a visited-config set, and unions all resulting file lists.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="adapter-step-number">03</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Let the compiler parse the complete program.</h3>
              <p>
                <InlineCode code="ts.createCompilerHost()" language="typescript" /> provides file
                and module-system operations.{' '}
                <InlineCode code="ts.createProgram()" language="typescript" />
                receives the union of configured root files and returns a
                <InlineCode code="Program" language="typescript" />. Its
                <InlineCode code="getSourceFiles()" language="typescript" /> output contains project
                files plus declarations and other files the compiler pulled in. That is why the real
                trace later reports 2 project files but 199 source files in the program.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="adapter-step-number">04</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Inspect the syntax this extractor supports.</h3>
              <p>
                The compiler has already converted each file into a
                <InlineCode code="SourceFile" language="typescript" /> syntax tree. At that root
                level, <InlineCode code="ts.forEachChild()" language="typescript" /> visits direct
                top-level statements.{' '}
                <InlineCode code="ts.isImportDeclaration()" language="typescript" />
                keeps static ES import declarations. Unlike Python's
                <InlineCode code="ast.walk()" language="python" />, this branch is not a recursive
                walk through every descendant and does not currently capture dynamic
                <InlineCode code="import()" language="typescript" />,
                <InlineCode code="require()" language="typescript" />, or re-export declarations.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="deep-code-pair deep-code-pair--foundations">
          <div class="deep-code">
            <p>
              <span>TypeScript</span> Abridged source: explicit or upward config discovery
            </p>
            <CodeWindow
