        <div class="adapter-panel-intro adapter-panel-intro--compact">
          <p class="deep-kicker">Python adapter</p>
          <h3>
            The AST describes <InlineCode code="..db" language="python" />; the resolver finds the
            concrete file.
          </h3>
          <p>
            <InlineCode code="_LocatedImport" language="python" /> is deliberately intermediate
            evidence. It knows what was written, where it appeared, and whether the syntax was
            relative, conditional, type-only, or dynamic. It cannot know the final target from
            syntax alone.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="python-edge-story" aria-label="One Python import becoming a graph edge">
          <article>
            <span>1 / Locate</span>
            <strong>
              <InlineCode code="src/ui/view.py" language="python" />
            </strong>
            <p>
              The outer file loop supplies the source identity. Inside that file, the parser finds
              <InlineCode code="from ..db import database" language="python" /> on line 12.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>2 / Classify</span>
            <strong>
              <InlineCode code="_LocatedImport" language="python" />
            </strong>
            <p>
              The record keeps <InlineCode code='module_name="..db"' language="python" />, line 12,
              alias <InlineCode code="database" language="python" />, and two kinds. The
              <InlineCode code="import_kind" language="python" /> describes context, while
              <InlineCode code="resolution_kind" language="python" /> preserves relative-path
              semantics even if the import is also conditional or type-only.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>3 / Resolve</span>
            <strong>
              <InlineCode code="src/db.py" language="python" />
            </strong>
            <p>
              Leading dots move from the importing package. The resolver tests a module file and
              then a package <InlineCode code="__init__.py" language="python" />. A path inside the
              discovered project becomes an internal target.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>4 / Record</span>
            <strong>
              <InlineCode code="Edge(view.py → db.py)" language="python" />
            </strong>
            <p>
              Only after resolution can ArchUnitPython store the importing path, resolved target,
              <InlineCode code="external=False" language="python" />, and the import kinds as one
              directed evidence record.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="resolution-detail">
          <div>
            <p class="deep-kicker">Python resolution in source</p>
            <h3>Resolve against files that actually exist.</h3>
            <p>
              Relative imports move from the source directory. Absolute imports are tested from the
              project root and its parent. One from-import can yield multiple namespace-package
              alias targets, so <InlineCode code="_resolve_import_targets()" language="python" />{' '}
              returns a list rather than one answer.
            </p>
            <p>
              The excerpt is abridged only around its enclosing loops. Every shown branch and record
              field comes from the current extractor.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="deep-code">
            <CodeWindow
              code={pythonResolution}
              filename="extract_graph.py · abridged source"
              language="python"
              copy
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="raw-graph-note">
          <h3>What Python records after resolution</h3>
          <p>
            The raw graph is <InlineCode code="Graph = list[Edge]" language="python" />. Each
            immutable edge stores a normalized absolute source path. Internal targets are absolute
            file paths too. An external target may remain a module identifier such as
            <InlineCode code="os" language="python" />, while an unresolved relative import or a
            module found outside the project root can remain a normalized absolute candidate path.
            The edge also carries an <InlineCode code="external" language="python" /> flag and
            import kinds such as
            <InlineCode code="relative" language="text" />,
            <InlineCode code="conditional" language="text" />, or
            <InlineCode code="type" language="text" />. There is no separate node table. A self-edge
            for every discovered file preserves files with no imports; equal source-target pairs are
            merged and their import kinds are combined.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

